    "text": "Suppose \\(L(x, y)\\) is the statement \"Student \\(x\\) solves question \\(y\\) correctly\".\nTranslate the statement into logical expression:\n\"For any question in the exam, there are at least two students who solve it correctly and at least one student who does not\".\n\n(i) \\(\\forall y(\\exists x(L(x, y) \\wedge \\exists x' L(x', y) \\wedge \\exists x'' \\neg L(x'', y)))\\)\n(ii) \\(\\forall y(\\exists x(L(x, y) \\wedge \\exists x' \\neg L(x', y)))\\)\n(iii) \\(\\forall y(\\exists x(L(x, y) \\wedge \\exists x'((x \\neq x') \\wedge L(x', y))))\\)\n(iv) \\(\\forall y(\\exists x(L(x, y) \\wedge \\exists x'((x \\neq x') \\wedge L(x', y))) \\wedge \\exists x'' \\neg L(x'', y))\\)",
